{"symbol":"NK.PA","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-16T18:24:46Z","info":{"address1":"43 Quai de Grenelle","city":"Paris","zip":"75015","country":"France","phone":"33 1 49 55 63 00","website":"https://www.imerys.com","industry":"Specialty Chemicals","industryKey":"specialty-chemicals","industryDisp":"Specialty Chemicals","sector":"Basic Materials","sectorKey":"basic-materials","sectorDisp":"Basic Materials","longBusinessSummary":"Imerys S.A. engages in the supply of specialty minerals for various industries across Europe, the Middle East, Africa, Asia Pacific, and America. The company offers performance minerals, such as additives for plastics, paints and coatings, filtration and life sciences, ceramics, and building products; specialty minerals used as processing aids for extreme work conditions, including refractory, foundry, abrasives, and building chemistry; and graphite and carbon minerals for energy transition and mobile energy markets. It also provides minerals, such as andalusite, ball clay, bentonite, calcium carbonate, carbon black, chamotte, diatomite, feldspar, fused alumina, graphite, halloysite, kaolin, lithium, mica, moler, mullite, perlite, quartz, talc, zeolite, zirconia, and wollastonite. The company serves various markets, such as abrasives, advanced ceramics, animal care, batteries and fuel cells, building materials, ceramics, component manufacturing, cosmetics and personal care, crop production, food and beverage, health, pharmaceuticals and biotechnology, home care, infrastructure and utilities, investment casting, pulp and packaging, and rubber markets. The company was incorporated in 1880 and is headquartered in Paris, France. Imerys S.A. is a subsidiary of Belgian Securities BV.","fullTimeEmployees":12300,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Alessandro  Dazza","age":56,"title":"Chief Executive Officer","yearBorn":1969,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1798365,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Pierre  Lebreuil